Troubleshooting:
----------------
## Issue 1 : 

When user is trying to login it is showing error message <br>
"**Too many attempts have been made to login. Please try again in 887 seconds.**"

**Reason:**<br>
So many failed login attempt have been made and due to this account is locked. <br>

<br>
You will get configurations from `config-backup/config/config.yaml` <br>
<br>

### Login postgres
```
# connect container:
docker exec -it postgresql bash

# Login postgres
psql postgresql://user:pass@postgresql/quay

# connect database
\c quay

# list tables
\dt
```

### Verify failed attempt:
```
SELECT
  username,
  enabled,
  invalid_login_attempts,
  last_invalid_login
FROM "user"
WHERE username = 'harshal';
```

### update failed attempt:
```
UPDATE "user"
SET
  invalid_login_attempts = 0,
  last_invalid_login = now() - interval '365 days',
  enabled = true
WHERE username = 'harshal';
```

## Issue 2 : Change password from backend:

### Generate Password HASH.
```
docker exec -it quay-app python3 - <<'EOF'
from bcrypt import hashpw, gensalt
print(hashpw(b"NewPassword123", gensalt()).decode())
EOF
```

### Then login postgres:
Connect postgres database same as above.
```
UPDATE "user"
SET password_hash = '<NEW_BCRYPT_HASH>'
WHERE username = '<username>';
```
